  "question": {
    "text": "If in nuclear fission, a piece of uranium of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>6.0</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is lost, the energy obtained (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kWh</mi></math>) is <math><mn>n</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Find the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1.25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#916;mc</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>4.5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>.5</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>13</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.6</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.25</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kWh</mi></math>",
